# User cancellation plus a five-second timeout

Save this as an HTML file and open it in a modern browser supporting both methods. Click Cancel before five seconds, or wait; reload to try again. This network-free example displays the combined signal’s reason.

```html
<!doctype html>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Combined cancellation</title>
<button id="cancel">Cancel</button>
<pre id="status">Waiting…</pre>
<script>
  const button = document.querySelector('#cancel');
  const output = document.querySelector('#status');
  const caller = new AbortController();
  const signal = AbortSignal.any([
    caller.signal,
    AbortSignal.timeout(5000)
  ]);
  button.onclick = () => caller.abort(
    new DOMException('Canceled by user', 'AbortError')
  );
  function showReason() {
    output.textContent = `${signal.reason.name}: ${signal.reason.message}`;
    button.disabled = true;
    button.onclick = null;
  }
  if (signal.aborted) showReason();
  else signal.addEventListener('abort', showReason, { once: true });
  // For a request, pass this signal: fetch(url, { signal });
</script>
```

**Documented behavior:** [MDN: AbortSignal.any()](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AbortSignal/any_static) says the combined signal takes the reason of the first input to abort. If inputs are already aborted at construction, it immediately uses the first already-aborted input in iterable order. Later aborts do not replace the winning reason. A caller’s custom reason is preserved, not automatically converted to `AbortError`.

[MDN: AbortSignal.timeout()](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AbortSignal/timeout_static) specifies milliseconds and a `TimeoutError` DOMException on timeout. **Application to this example (inference):** cancellation first yields our explicit `AbortError`; timeout first yields `TimeoutError`. Combining signals does not cancel the losing timeout.

**Limitation:** MDN specifies *active time*, not elapsed wall time: the timeout pauses in suspended workers or while a document is in the back-forward cache. **Inference:** this is not a strict five-second wall-clock deadline.

